# Install-context path defaults, in the one format both consumers read: each
# line a plain KEY=value assignment, so systemd units take this file as an
# EnvironmentFile= and bash scripts source it. Keep it that way -- one
# assignment per line, no exports, no arrays, no shell syntax.
#
# These are the DEFAULTS. ctx_from_env (context.sh) can move any of them --
# target_mount and pre-mount configs move the target off /mnt -- and writes
# the resolved values to $CTX_STATE_DIR/context.env. A unit that needs the
# live context layers the two:
#   EnvironmentFile=/usr/share/omarchy-iso/orchestrator/context.env
#   EnvironmentFile=-/run/omarchy-install/context.env
# (later files win; the dash tolerates the runtime file not existing yet).

CTX_TARGET=/mnt
CTX_OMARCHY_PATH=/usr/share/omarchy
CTX_STATE_DIR=/run/omarchy-install
CTX_LOG_PATH=/var/log/omarchy-install.log
